AC2 evidence — NEARS-3327 — scandir() absolute-path fix verified from a non-project-root CWD

Method: invoked the ACTUAL fixed AddonController::getDirectories() method (post-fix, base_path()
applied) from a raw PHP process whose CWD was deliberately set to /private/tmp (not the project
root), bootstrapping the real worktree's Laravel container. Paired with a negative control: the
same relative scandir('Modules') call WITHOUT the fix's base_path() wrapping, from the identical
CWD.

--- Control (pre-fix relative-path behavior, same CWD) ---
$ cd /private/tmp && php -r '
    chdir("/private/tmp");
    echo "cwd: " . getcwd() . "\n";
    $items = @scandir("Modules");
    if ($items === false) { echo "scandir FAILED (relative path, non-project-root CWD)\n"; }
    else { print_r($items); }
  '
cwd: /private/tmp
scandir FAILED (relative path, non-project-root CWD)

--- Post-fix (actual AddonController::getDirectories('Modules'), same CWD) ---
$ cd /private/tmp && php /path/to/nears3327-cwd-check.php
  (bootstraps /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-3327-system-addons-500/Admin, instantiates
   App\Http\Controllers\Admin\System\AddonController, calls ->getDirectories('Modules'))

CWD at call time: /private/tmp
getDirectories('Modules') result:
Array
(
    [0] => AI
    [1] => TaxModule
)

Interpretation: with CWD != project root, the pre-fix relative scandir('Modules') call fails
outright (control, reproduces the reported defect). The actual post-fix getDirectories(), which
wraps $path in base_path($path) before scandir(), correctly resolves the absolute path from the
identical non-project-root CWD and returns the real installed module/addon directories, including
AI (the expected installed addon directory named in the AC) and TaxModule — confirming the
absolute-path fix holds independent of PHP's working directory.
